<h2 id="abstract">Abstract</h2>
<p class="wp-abstract">Modern foundation models can generate remarkably capable responses, yet the invocation of a model is fundamentally episodic: each inference is assembled from model weights plus the state supplied at that moment. Products can add memory, tools, profiles, and agent loops around that inference, but persistent storage alone does not establish longitudinal cognition. LUNA - Longitudinal Unified Narrative Architecture - is a research and engineering project exploring a stronger systems question: what happens when the artificial system interpreting the present has itself been causally altered by what happened before?</p>
<p class="wp-abstract">LUNA separates the persistent system from the replaceable inference substrate and organizes cognition across multiple timescales: evidence-grounded memory, associative availability, goal and prospective state, appraisal, slower global modulation, volitional action selection, perception with environmental continuity, reflection, and developmental consolidation. The key distinction is between remembering an experience and being changed by it. A formative event may eventually become less retrievable while its effects persist in prediction, attention, motivation, relationship models, dispositions, habits, or self-model.</p>
<p class="wp-abstract">The project does not treat these architectural hypotheses as evidence of phenomenal consciousness. Instead, it proposes falsifiable longitudinal tests. ChronoForge, LUNA&#x27;s planned temporal development and evaluation infrastructure, is designed to begin from controlled checkpoints, vary developmental conditions, architecture, model substrate, or developmental timing, and measure later divergence in the histories that emerge under declared conditions. This white paper defines that research thesis, describes the public conceptual architecture, reports the current prototype boundary, presents early observations that exposed key gaps, and outlines a program for controlled longitudinal evaluation.</p>
<p><strong>Keywords: </strong>longitudinal AI, cognitive architecture, persistent memory, artificial development, associative cognition, experiential learning, agent memory, ChronoForge</p>
<h2 id="the-proposition-at-a-glance">The Proposition at a Glance</h2>
<div class="wp-callout"><strong>CENTRAL CONTRAST  </strong>Most AI systems are assembled from the information available to them now. LUNA investigates what changes when the system interpreting the present has itself been altered by what happened before.</div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>1</span><div><p><strong>Capability is not continuity<br /></strong>A powerful model can reason well without possessing a persistent causal history. LUNA treats those as different properties.</p></div></div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>2</span><div><p><strong>Memory is necessary but insufficient<br /></strong>A system can store and retrieve an episode perfectly yet remain behaviorally indistinguishable from a branch in which the episode never occurred.</p></div></div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>3</span><div><p><strong>Development requires multiple timescales<br /></strong>Immediate interpretation, recent activation, persistent memory, ongoing concerns, internal state, future commitments, action consequences, and slower structural change must interact without collapsing into one prompt.</p></div></div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>4</span><div><p><strong>Experience is causally different from data<br /></strong>In experience, the running participant chooses actions, consequences arrive later, actors and projects recur, and the resulting history can change the participant.</p></div></div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>5</span><div><p><strong>Continuity should survive substrate changes<br /></strong>The persistent instance should not be identical to one model, provider, machine, or device. LUNA names the persistent continuity state the Stack and the replaceable computational substrate the Sleeve.</p></div></div>
<div class="wp-proposition"><span>6</span><div><p><strong>The claims are experimentally approachable<br />Identical starting states can enter different controlled developmental conditions - or the same conditions under different model sleeves, architectural topologies, or developmental timing - and the histories that emerge can then be compared under neutral post-development probes.</strong></p></div></div>
