<h2 id="associative-cognition-and-ongoing-mental-availability">4. Associative Cognition and Ongoing Mental Availability</h2>
<p>Ordinary retrieval is externally driven: a user asks about a topic and the system searches for relevant history. LUNA&#x27;s associative-cognition direction asks what happens next. A surfaced memory may itself become a cue. A conclusion, question, plan, or realization may make other material more available. In that sense, cognition becomes part of the system&#x27;s own environment.</p>
<p>The project uses the term Reverie for internally triggered associative recall. The intended mechanism is bounded and competitive rather than recursively walking the entire memory graph. Most potentially relevant material should remain latent; only a small subset should become foreground cognition.</p>
<div class="wp-callout"><strong>DESIGN PRINCIPLE  </strong>Memory can remind memory. Cognition can trigger cognition. But activation is not the same thing as consciousness, and associative propagation is not permission for unbounded recursive inference.</div>
<p>A related concept is a recent-life horizon: a compact representation of what has been happening lately - important episodes, unresolved threads, active projects, and meaningful changes - without replaying full transcripts into every model call. This preserves continuity while controlling context growth.</p>
<h2 id="multiple-timescales-appraisal-persistent-state-and-future-orientation">5. Multiple Timescales: Appraisal, Persistent State, and Future Orientation</h2>
<p>A longitudinal architecture cannot treat every event as isolated. What an event means now and what state the system remains in afterward are different questions. LUNA&#x27;s architecture separates immediate appraisal from slower homeostatic-style modulation and from still slower dispositional or developmental change.</p>
<h3 id="5-1-appraisal">5.1 Appraisal</h3>
<p>Appraisal evaluates structured aspects of an event such as novelty, expectedness, self- or goal-relevance, controllability, and agency. In the current prototype, appraisal exists as a shadow diagnostic layer: it can observe and record evaluations without causally changing memory, personality, retrieval, or action selection. This makes it possible to validate semantics before granting the subsystem behavioral power.</p>
<h3 id="5-2-homeostatic-modulation">5.2 Homeostatic modulation</h3>
<p>The proposed Homeostatic Modulation System is an endocrine-like analogy, not a claim that software possesses literal hormones or human emotions. The intended role is to carry bounded, decaying operating-state effects across multiple later cognitive episodes. Repeated failure, sustained uncertainty, success, overload, novelty, or social interaction could alter later attention, confidence, verification, exploration, or recovery pressure without requiring the original event to be injected into each prompt.</p>
<div class="wp-callout"><strong>ENVIRONMENTAL PRINCIPLE  </strong>Do not instruct the model to “act stressed,” “be confident,” or “be curious.” Change persistent internal conditions, let those conditions modulate cognition, and observe what behavior follows.</div>
<h3 id="5-3-prospective-cognition">5.3 Prospective cognition</h3>
<p>A persistent mind-like system also needs a future, not only a past. Prospective cognition represents unresolved intentions, expected events, deadlines, anticipated opportunities, and conditions that may become relevant later. The architectural goal is for time to become causally meaningful even when the user is not currently asking about it.</p>